  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"A missed pickup can be held for one more service period, and the reader can be contacted.\", \"decision\": \"What should happen when a reader misses a pickup window?\", \"goal\": \"Keep books moving and make the afternoon service easier to use without excluding readers who arrive without an appointment.\", \"problem\": \"A small library becomes crowded during afternoon pickups and returns. It has a request sheet, adjustable pickup windows, a few trained helpers, labeled shelves, and enough room to separate several activities. Staff want a practical plan that preserves walk-in access. Each decision below concerns a different part of the service; none requires exclusive use of all helpers or space.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nStaff contact the reader with the remaining pickup windows and move the book only after the reader selects one. The reader chooses among the remaining spaces before the extra hold is arranged.\nStaff contact the reader to agree on a new pickup window before moving the book to the next period’s holding shelf. The extra hold follows a confirmed intention to collect.\nStaff move the book to the next period’s holding shelf and then contact the reader with the new pickup window. The book remains available while the reader receives a default second opportunity."
    }
